// Economies of scale, part 1 (docs/specs/phase7/economies-of-scale.md 4.1, 5; P7-ES1): division of labour, crowding, span of control, the manufactory licence. Money in mites.
// grades_pm: the permille of a recipe's worker-hours done by the master's steps, the journeyman's steps and the apprentice's or hand's steps (sum 1,000). A recipe with no row is all hand steps (no division).
// A row names a recipe id (wins) or a skill; weaving 100/300/600, tailoring 200/400/400, brewing 200/300/500, carpentry 150/450/400 (sawing 0/300/700), charcoal 0/200/800, brick moulding 50/150/800.
